{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"4-ARM RESULTS, BOTH RUNS ADJUDICATED - the cleanest comparison in the study and a materially worse result for rebar than the supplementary panels reported. Identical input, concurrent execution, same three judges per run, one pass. Agreement was the highest recorded: Fleiss kappa 0.856 on carbon and 0.900 on uswds, zero contested items across 156 ballot rows and 204 relation candidates. POOLED BY DISTINCT ISSUE: Compound Engineering 59 true positives, 0 false positives, 100 percent precision, 84 percent materiality; superpowers 28 true positives, 0 false positives, 100 percent precision, 80 percent materiality; mini-swe-agent 17 true positives, 1 false positive, 94 percent precision, 89 percent materiality and the highest materiality of any arm; rebar 18 true positives, 3 false positives, 86 percent precision, 69 percent materiality - last on both, and the only arm whose row count overstates its issue count, at plus 21 percent. WHY THIS DIVERGES FROM THE 93.2 PERCENT PRECISION THE WAVE 3 SUPPLEMENTARY PANELS GAVE REBAR: those panels judged rebar's findings ALONE against a frozen reference set built without it, so the comparative question was never asked. Here rebar's rows sit on the same ballot as CE's, and a judge assessing materiality does so beside dozens of well-grounded competitor findings. This is not judges being harsher - agreement was higher, not lower. CAVEATS TO CARRY WITH THE NUMBERS: two runs only, both large epics with sub-issues drawn from the replacement set, so not a random sample. The nine Wave 3 runs remain the larger evidence for rebar's absolute behaviour; these two are the better evidence for relative standing."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789447464949274001,"uuid":"5ef84334-a9a9-4207-92a9-767bfefcc722"}